# SQLite migrations (backend/migrations)

Migrations run **inside a transaction** with **foreign_keys ON** (see `internal/db/migrate.go` + `db.Open`). Write SQL accordingly.

## Hard rules

1. **Never `DROP TABLE` a table that is referenced with `ON DELETE CASCADE`** (e.g. `player`, `player_race`, `tournament`, `tournament_player`, `fantasy_*`) unless you have explicitly rebuilt **all** dependents in the same migration and verified no data loss.
2. **`PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF` is a no-op inside a migration transaction** — do not rely on it to make DROP/rebuild “safe”.
3. Prefer **additive** changes: `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX`, `ALTER TABLE … ADD COLUMN`.
4. Changing a column DEFAULT only: **do not rebuild the table**. App code / `INSERT` defaults are enough for new rows; leave existing rows alone unless a deliberate data backfill is required.
5. If a table rebuild is unavoidable:
   - Copy rows with **explicit `id` columns** preserved
   - Recreate every dependent FK target with matching IDs before re-enabling reliance on FKs
   - Prefer a **new migration file** that only adds a parallel table + backfill + cutover, never a casual DROP of a hot parent table
6. **Do not edit already-applied migrations** on shared/prod DBs. Fix forward with a new numbered file. Editing is OK only if you are sure the version was never applied anywhere that matters.
7. Name files `NNN_snake_case.sql` (next integer after the latest). Bump `migrate_test.go` expected version when adding a file.
8. Comment **why** a risky step is safe (or that it is intentionally additive-only).

## Examples

```sql
-- ✅ additive
CREATE TABLE player_import_queue (…);
ALTER TABLE user_title ADD COLUMN date TEXT;

-- ❌ wipes tournament_player / fantasy via ON DELETE CASCADE when FKs are on
DROP TABLE player_race;
```

```sql
-- ❌ useless inside migrate tx — FK still enforced
PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;
DROP TABLE player_race;
```

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] No `DROP`/`TRUNCATE` of parent tables with CASCADE children unless data-preserving rebuild is proven
- [ ] No dependence on `PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF` inside the migration
- [ ] Fresh migrate test still passes (`go test ./internal/db/`)
